WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.435
-Welcome back to
the show, buddy.

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:03.569
It's so good to see you,

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:05.104
and thanks for playing
that game with me.

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:06.872
-Oh, yeah. Anytime.

00:00:06.872 --> 00:00:08.941
-I knew that you were levels --
You're levels above.

00:00:08.941 --> 00:00:10.743
You were already
playing the game

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:12.445
probably before it even
came out there.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:14.981
-Yeah, I'm like a --
Yeah, I like to plan ahead.

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:17.417
I'm like a criminal mastermind.
-Yeah, you really are, yeah.

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:18.585
-Yeah.

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:21.554
-I have a thousand things
I want to ask you about.

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:24.090
I know you probably can't tell
me much about "Stranger Things."

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.391
-Yeah.
-Season 4, right?

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:26.392
What can you say?

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:28.628
-Well, we --
What I can say is, like,

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.563
we just did literally 300 --

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:33.599
We just finished shooting,
and it was Day 300.

00:00:33.599 --> 00:00:36.369
-What?
-Yeah. We shot for 300 days.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:37.436
-Holy moly!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.436 --> 00:00:41.174
Is it a longer --
-The audience claps.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:44.110
None of the crew was clapping.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.244
-They're exhausted.

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:47.379
-They were like,
"Alright, cool, guys.

00:00:47.379 --> 00:00:50.383
Yeah, cool. Yeah, we'll leave."

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:51.717
No, but it's great.
-Wow!

00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:54.353
-Yeah, it was a long --
-Those Duffer brothers, huh?

00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:58.257
-Yeah. Like, I'm so glad they
still care, 'cause, you know,

00:00:58.257 --> 00:01:00.927
if a show runs for that long,
the creators stop caring.

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:01.961
They cash in.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.596
And they really still care.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:04.997
-Yeah. You can tell.

00:01:04.997 --> 00:01:07.100
It's quality stuff.
Last season was awesome.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.902
-Yeah. Yeah, the show
is going to be --

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:12.037
It's going to be
really messed up this season.

00:01:12.037 --> 00:01:14.841
-Well, I wanted to
test your poker face,

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:16.342
'cause I know we just
played "True Confessions."

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:20.613
So I will -- I'm gonna just say
four rumors about this season

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:22.481
and then I want to see your
reaction and see --

00:01:22.481 --> 00:01:23.582
-Oh, yeah. Okay, cool.

00:01:23.582 --> 00:01:25.585
-And we'll see if
it's real or not.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:28.955
-Yeah, sure.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:32.358
-Will we find out what happened
to Hopper this season?

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:34.594
Okay.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:36.796
♪♪

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:39.265
How about Mike and Eleven?

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:40.934
Are they going to reunite?

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.201
-Oh...

00:01:42.201 --> 00:01:44.203
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:47.006
-"Oh" is the funniest answer.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:51.444
Will we see Eleven
get her powers back?

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:53.346
-But...

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:54.914
-Yeah.

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:57.684
Who are the Creels

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:59.752
and what's their connection
to the Upside Down?

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.622
Okay. There you go right there.
That's it.

00:02:03.622 --> 00:02:04.657
That's how you do it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:06.725
-Thank you.
♪♪

00:02:06.725 --> 00:02:08.260
Thank you.

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:09.728
Thank you.
Thank you so much.

00:02:09.728 --> 00:02:10.730
-Thank you for playing
along with that.

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.031
-Yeah.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.666
-I want to talk about your music
for a little bit here.

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:16.002
-Yeah.
-This is your album cover.

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.270
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:18.971
I love the art.
-Yeah.

00:02:18.971 --> 00:02:20.506
-What is it?
Is this is an artist?

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:22.241
A famous artist?

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:24.878
-No, it's the drummer
in my band.

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:26.612
It's me and my friend
Malcolm Craig,

00:02:26.612 --> 00:02:27.847
and Malcolm did the cover art.

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:29.182
He's an amazing artist.
-That's fantastic.

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:30.216
I love it.
-Yeah.

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:32.251
-The name of the album is
"Karaoke Alone."

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:34.820
-Yeah. Yeah.
-I have done that, yeah.

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.956
-Yeah. Oh, that's sad.

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:37.957
-Thank you.

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.292
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:40.593
-Someone asked me that question?

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.028
They were like, "Have you ever
done karaoke alone?"

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:43.429
And I was like...
-Of course.

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:44.463
-..."No, no."

00:02:44.463 --> 00:02:45.798
-Well, not really karaoke,

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.232
but you probably sang
in your bedroom or something.

00:02:47.232 --> 00:02:48.234
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.536
But I mean,
like, karaoke bar alone.

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:52.438
Like, I just imagine you, like,

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:55.241
disheveled after a day of work,
by yourself in a karaoke --

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:57.443
-Glass of whiskey?
-Yeah, in your -- By yourself.

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:59.211
-Beer. Yeah, sing...

00:02:59.211 --> 00:03:03.149
♪ All by myself ♪

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:04.884
I'm trying to think
if I ever have.

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:06.886
It sounds like something I might
have done just to, like --

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:08.988
I think I had to, like,
practice for some --

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:10.290
I had to do an
impression of something.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.657
-And had to go, maybe, yeah.

00:03:11.657 --> 00:03:13.526
-Well, in my apartment,
everyone can hear everything,

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:16.195
so I went to a karaoke place to
practice my impression

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:17.430
of Bruce Springsteen
or something.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.831
-Yeah.
-Just so I can go like -- Yeah.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:21.601
Because my neighbor will be
like, "Go to bed!"

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:22.768
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:23.936
-So I probably did
go to karaoke alone.

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:25.338
-A very New York neighbor
of yours.

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:27.173
-Yeah, exactly. Right?
Exactly, yeah.

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:30.309
But let's talk you about --
Because The Aubreys

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:31.311
is the name of your band.

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:32.611
-Yeah.

00:03:32.611 --> 00:03:33.679
-Were you all ways called
The Aubreys?

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:34.747
No. You were in
a different band.

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:35.782
-Yeah, I was in
a different band before,

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:37.550
and then I formed this band.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.218
And then it was going to be
called The Audreys,

00:03:39.218 --> 00:03:41.320
and then there was another band
from Australia, I think,

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.354
called The Audreys.

00:03:42.354 --> 00:03:43.656
And then I said,
"Wouldn't it be funny

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:45.291
if we just swapped the
'D' to a 'B'?"

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:48.394
And we started laughing.
And then we did.

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:49.795
-Dude, that's the way to do it.
-So -- Yeah.

00:03:49.795 --> 00:03:51.363
-So The Aubreys
is the name of the group.

00:03:51.363 --> 00:03:52.498
-Yeah.
-I love it.

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:53.833
-Yeah.
-Great name.

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:55.101
-"Karaoke Alone."

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:56.135
Do we know
when it is coming out?

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.703
-Yeah, November 5th.

00:03:57.703 --> 00:03:59.104
-Oh, wow!
-Yeah.

00:03:59.104 --> 00:04:00.206
-Big month.
-Yeah.

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:01.440
Yeah.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.843
-You have a big month,
November, 'cause, dude,

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:06.178
you're relaunching, rebooting
the new "Ghostbusters."

00:04:06.178 --> 00:04:07.180
-I am.
-Congrats on that.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:08.615
-Thank you.

00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:12.118
Yeah, it's actually kind of
almost, like, a direct sequel,

00:04:12.118 --> 00:04:13.453
but it's, like, made --

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:17.023
I mean, obviously,
the original came out in '84.

00:04:17.023 --> 00:04:20.259
And, yeah, Jason Reitman
is writing and directing it,

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:21.360
who's Ivan --

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.963
-His son.
-Yeah, it's his son.

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:27.399
And it's, like, a really amazing
kind of family affair.

00:04:27.399 --> 00:04:28.901
-Your family moves
into this, like,

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:31.804
in the middle of some farm that
their dad -- her dad left her.

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:32.872
-Right, right.

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:34.107
-Her dad is Harold Ramis'
character.

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:35.440
-Correct.

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:38.210
-And you get to this
farm and you're hanging around,

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.113
playing and you go --
Is it under the garage?

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:41.246
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:41.246 --> 00:04:44.082
Mckenna Grace,
who's an incredible actor,

00:04:44.082 --> 00:04:46.152
plays my little sister,
kind of starts to uncover

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:48.220
some spooky stuff.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:49.789
-Yeah.
Then you find the Ecto-1, dude.

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:52.659
-Yeah, I find
the Ecto-1 in a garage.

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:54.860
-Dude, you get to drive
the Ecto-1?

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.395
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:56.395 --> 00:04:57.529
Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:57.529 --> 00:04:59.331
-I mean, it's so --
That's pretty cool.

00:04:59.331 --> 00:05:00.433
-It is really cool.

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:02.268
-And you got to meet
the original cast?

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:04.236
-I did. Yeah. Yeah.
It was nuts.

00:05:04.236 --> 00:05:06.506
-I mean, you can't --
Dan Aykroyd and Bill Murray --

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:08.474
you can't get better,
nicer people.

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:11.110
-No, that's what's crazy
is that they were, like --

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.412
It's like being
in the room with, like,

00:05:13.412 --> 00:05:14.646
the Apostles or something.

00:05:14.646 --> 00:05:17.683
Like, you don't, like -- It's --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.683 --> 00:05:18.817
Like, I don't know
if that it makes sense,

00:05:18.817 --> 00:05:20.953
but, like, it's weird.

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:23.089
It's like seeing,
like, you know,

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:25.124
Bill, like, you know,
leading the charge.

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:27.627
It's, like, really --
And I just called him Bill

00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:28.828
like I know him really well.

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:29.962
-Yeah.

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:32.298
-You know, when Billy led
the charge on set,

00:05:32.298 --> 00:05:33.532
it was so awesome.

00:05:33.532 --> 00:05:34.666
When we were at Nobu together,
it was so cool.

00:05:34.666 --> 00:05:38.971
-He does have a magnetic --
a magnetism.

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:40.173
So does Dan Aykroyd, as well.
-Yeah.

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:42.441
He makes everything he's
ever in better.

00:05:42.441 --> 00:05:44.844
-Yeah, I agree.
Both of -- But you, too, bud.

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:46.212
-Oh, thank you.
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:46.212 --> 00:05:47.446
-Yeah.

00:05:47.446 --> 00:05:49.615
-Here's Finn Wolfhard in
"Ghostbusters: Afterlife."

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:50.750
Take a look.

00:05:53.652 --> 00:05:55.087
-Is that a...

00:05:55.087 --> 00:05:57.289
-Free-floating metal muncher.

00:05:57.289 --> 00:05:58.558
Definitely Class 5.

00:05:58.558 --> 00:06:00.893
-Okay.
-Uh...what do we do?

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:02.528
-Let's get him.

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:03.529
-What?!

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:05.365
-I'm gonna get a photo first.

00:06:08.333 --> 00:06:09.668
-Guys...

00:06:09.668 --> 00:06:11.371
-Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:06:12.838 --> 00:06:13.839
-[ Gasps ]

00:06:13.839 --> 00:06:14.941
-It has a gunner's seat?

00:06:21.614 --> 00:06:23.649
[ Creaking ]

00:06:26.519 --> 00:06:28.020
-Go, go, go!

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.121
[ Tires squeal ]

00:06:29.121 --> 00:06:32.524
-Yeah! Finn Wolfhard!

00:06:32.524 --> 00:06:36.161
"Ghostbusters: Afterlife"
is in theaters November 19th.

00:06:36.161 --> 00:06:38.064
Go check out his album by
The Aubreys, everybody.

